Where there are annoyances there are also opportunities to create services. So the natural consequence is that someone says: What if I set up an industrial warehouse full of powerful machines dedicated to mining and I offer people the possibility of hiring the power they want?
Hashflare was founded by Sergei Potapenko in 2014 and is located in Tallinn, Estonia. It is a country with prices per Kw / h for industrial electrical energy that are quite convenient compared to many other countries in the European Union, which is undoubtedly interesting.
The contracts are for one year, so you will choose the initial power you want to contract and you will pay at once for 12 months.
When it comes to paying there are different methods. You can pay in Bitcoin or also by bank transfer and others including paying with the positive balance that you have obtained by mining.
Pools are groups of miners who cooperate to provide computational power or hashrate and then the profits are distributed proportionally.
It is certainly an advantage that Hashflare allows you to choose the pools to which you want to connect your contracted power. Other cloud mining services do not provide this option.
It is recommended that you start with one or more of these, the largest and, in any case, collect information on each of them. It is convenient for you, as you will expect to connect to pools that work properly and no doubt about your honesty.
You are going to hire a service for a year but there is no guarantee that you will get rich. Not even that you're going to win something.
The variables at stake are many but, naturally, if you want to mine some of the most desired cryptocurrencies, the main options you have are the following:
Buy a computer and rent a space in a data center that keeps it running 24 hours and cross your fingers so it doesn't get spoiled.
A higher contracted power, more likely to mine blocks. I already tell you from the start, with little power you will get bored.
If we take into account the above and, particularly, the third variable, we cannot say that investing in cloud mining is going to be a quiet investment. Let's try to make some rough calculation based on the current situation.
I already anticipate that if you hire the minimum, as it appears on the Hashflare website, you would obtain a miniscule profit in the best of cases. If anything, a few dollars at the end of the year, with maintenance fees discounted.
Therefore, your initial investment should be much larger if you want to do something here.
However when I speak of net profit I keep in mind the return on investment and the maintenance commission that, remember, it is $ 0,0035 per day and for every 10 GH / s, which represents a very interesting figure for the company and not so much for you since that is going to be one of the reasons why your final profit is significantly less. In the previous case I have been somewhat conservative since the main factor is the value of the cryptocurrency.
Nor can you take these calculations as something statistically true and immovable. Not only may I have erred at some point (I assume it, but surely someone will be able to correct me in the comments) but, as I said, the variable value of Bitcoin as well as the speed or slowness of its rise or fall weigh too much.
You may have realized that the configuration of the plan you hire is very importantDepending on what you want to do or achieve, it will be, of course, to obtain the maximum return for your investment. If you are interested in my opinion, I will suggest the strategy that I think is the most interesting.
Of course, if you have read this article to the end, it is because the subject interests you a lot. Maybe you should try it yourself by starting with a prudent investment.
