This new market for virtual currencies was a real boom a few years ago, when the value of its most illustrious currency, Bitcoin, soared, achieving great popularity and catching regulators completely off guard. Precisely, the main difference of this market with respect to the traditional one is that is not controlled -for now- by any official institution.
The first thing to understand is that when we invest through contracts for differences in any asset, be it stocks, commodities, currencies, we do not physically own it but rather we agree with the seller that the underlying asset will go up or down. price in a certain period of time.
Trading cryptocurrencies through CFDs also has the advantage that you can do it with leverage, which may be more or less high depending on whether you are a professional or a retail trader. This means that the trader does not need a very high capital to start trading but can do so with only a percentage of the total value of the position.
Another plus point is that it can be operated 24 hours a day, seven days a week. In addition, it provides greater security than when operating directly with cryptocurrencies if we use a regulated and professional broker.
The above is a simple explanation but the concept goes much further. Let's see some of its main characteristics:
Decentralized: there is no central body that issues or controls them. This feature is definitely innovative since somehow democratize money that, until now, it was always something controlled by certain organisms or economic elites.
All transactions are recorded in hundreds or thousands of "ledgers" that must be exactly the same. If by some artifice I create or transfer some Bitcoin that is not reflected in those account books distributed all over the world, simply my "Bitcoin" will not be accepted and, therefore, it is virtually impossible for me to do this trick.
This means that when a transaction has been made there is no going back; with some nuances as we will see in future articles. What is clear is that Bitcoin transactions are much safer (and faster) than a bank transfer or payment systems such as Paypal.
Ultimately, Bitcoin is a currency and can be used exactly the same as any other currency that really has some value.
Resounding rises and falls has already had a few, although each time its price has shot up and then fell sharply, it has always been above previous values. It is logical; remember, it is a rare currency: there will only be 21 million Bitcoin and, despite everything, some will have been lost along the way.
It is virtually impossible to control transactions made from one person's wallet to someone else's. Thus, regulatory bodies have a long way to go while the invention of new methods and systems runs much faster.
Is it true that Bitcoin is used for criminal acts?
In that it is not different from the Euros, about which we do not usually ask ourselves these existential doubts. If I hire an assassin and accept Bitcoin as payment, it is clear that I can do it.
The idea is that they were practically instantaneous; then the reality is different but for that there are also many options in electronic currencies. What is quite clear is that sending money from one place to another in the world by wire transfer is noticeably slower.
Saving your savings is tremendously easier with Bitcoin. And sure, although I understand that there are people who still believe that banks are more so.
If you are living a complicated situation, Bitcoin they cannot be seized from you.
I hope I have clarified some concepts about Bitcoin in this article but we will go much deeper in successive publications. I believe that it is very important that we do not give up knowing in depth this explosion of financial and economic creativity that decentralized electronic currencies are giving us.
