Bitstamp is a Slovenian exchange that reported the theft of 2015 Bitcoin in January 19000 (about $ 5 million at the time). Despite the fact that, apparently, it did not return the money, it has continued to operate and maintain the trust of its users by implementing accessory security measures in the form of multi-signature wallets, which cannot transfer funds unless they are signed by the Exchange.
