Of these 7,5 million, more than 60% have bought cryptocurrencies as an investment and speculation mechanism, while 12,8% declare they use them to buy goods and services.
The average Spanish citizen who owns cryptocurrencies would be a male between 18 and 34 years old with a high annual economic income, which would go between the 100.000 to more than 500.000 euros.
