The Origin of the ‘Twelve Days of Christmas ’
However , did you know that the song was written to allow Catholic parents to teach their faith to their sons and daughters in secret ?
Two turtle doves : the Old Testament and the New Testament .
Four calling birds : the four Gospel writers : Matthew , Mark , Luke , and John .
Six geese a-laying : the six days that it took God to make creation .
Twelve drummers drumming : the twelve points of doctrine in the Apostles ’ Creed .
The next time you hear or sing this song , think of all the great gifts God has given us .
( Lucy learned this from her fifth-grade teacher at her Catholic school. )
The staff at 2 fish.co is happy to announce our site’s newest feature : publishing each day’s readings and Gospel .
We are taking the readings from our on-line Bible , which is the Catholic Public Domain Version – a recent , original edition by Ronald L .
Other sites publish daily readings , too , but we doubt if they look as good on a smart phone .
We hope to shortly make these readings available through a daily email , too .
( Don’t worry , she is not staying until midnight to publish it. )
Our site’s name has two meanings : we hope that our reasoned , positive explanation of the faith and its practices will attract those interested in it .
In addition , we hope to make a lot with limited resources – like the miracle of the five loaves and the 2 fish .
complete many of the reference links ( from articles to the bible pages ),
If you are interested in helping , or would like to provide feedback or simply say ‘hello ’ or wish us luck , please use our contact form .
