The Origin of the ‘Twelve Days of Christmas’ – 2fish
The Origin of the ‘Twelve Days of Christmas’
Have you ever heard the song ‘The Twelve Days of Christmas ?’ Of course , you have !
Why in secret ?
So , Catholic parents used symbols such as the three french hens and five golden rings to represent different parts of the faith .
Here are all the Twelve Days and their meanings :
He was a carpenter who worked with wood and died on a wooden cross .
Three French hens : the Three Theological Virtues : Faith , Hope , and Love .
Five golden rings : the five books of the Torah : Genesis , Exodus , Leviticus , Numbers , and Deuteronomy .
Seven swans a-swimming : the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit .
Nine ladies a-dancing : the nine fruits of the Holy Spirit
These are the meanings of each of the gifts .
