Loading should be faster than in the past, and legibility (or readability) and navigation have been improved, too.
Images should look good on both normal and retina screens; however, our only remaining task is to edit each image (the art work) to make it fully responsive, too.
Please note that we have designed the messages to look best on (newer) mobile phones.
The daily readings are published by 11-year-old Lucy, who has been doing an excellent job for almost one year!
The next time you hear or sing this song, think of all the great gifts God has given us.
(Lucy learned this from her fifth-grade teacher at her Catholic school.)
Each day at midnight (EST) time, that day’s Catholic Mass reading(s) and Gospel will be published.
(In the true spirit of the faith, Mr. Conte makes it available for free and without restriction.)
For now, though, we want to thank eleven-year-old Lucy Spero for volunteering to perform the work.
God Bless, and if you like the new feature, please let us know.
We still have a lot of work to do and are looking for like-minded volunteers to:
contribute articles about Catholicism and the bible,
contribute articles to defend the Faith against current attacks,
contribute financially (if the site is successful and needs its own hosting account).
