Ultimately , it attests not to her holiness , moreover , but to the holiness of Jesus , on whose account she received special prerogatives .
Certainly one can see God’s loving wisdom in affirming Mary’s bodily resurrection to the world at the midpoint of a century that witnessed so many grave injustices against the dignity of the human person .
The nobility of woman and her chief vocation of motherhood have especially been assaulted by modern society , which has focused inordinately upon her exterior beauty and sought ever to reduce her to an object of lust .
