Jesus ’ sacrifice is not an event confined to the distant past .
So , in the celebration of the Eucharist , God , who is outside of space and time , makes the sacrifice of Jesus present to the assembly of His people , re-presenting it to us in an unbloody manner .
This is why Saint Paul wrote in his First Letter to the Corinthians 10:16, “The cup of blessing that we bless , is it not a participation in the blood of Christ ?
” This is the ineffable joy and mystery of the Mass , in which we receive the fullness of the love of Jesus .
