” At this point , the Apostle Simon steps forward to speak on behalf of the Twelve , giving the correct answer : “You are the Christ , the Son of the living God.” To this , Jesus responds :
For flesh and blood has not revealed this to you , but my Father who is in heaven .
Second , in verse 18, He gives Simon his new name , Peter , fulfilling His words to him from the Gospel of John 1:42.
Third , in verse 19, Jesus gives Peter the gift of the keys of the kingdom of heaven and the authority to bind and loose ( in rabbinical language this meant to forbid and permit ), assuring him that his earthly decisions would be upheld in heaven .
The things which Peter teaches on earth will be upheld as truths by God in heaven .
This special grace is what Catholics call Papal Infallibility .
