11:8 You , O Lord , will preserve us , and you will guard us from this generation into eternity .
Will you forget me until the end ?
12:2 How long can I take counsel in my soul , sorrowing in my heart throughout the day ?
12:5 lest at any time my enemy may say , “I have prevailed against him.” Those who trouble me will exult , if I have been disturbed .
My heart will exult in your salvation .
And I will sing psalms to the name of the Lord Most High .
There is no one who does good ; there is not even one .
13:3 They have all gone astray ; together they have become useless .
13:4 Their throat is an open sepulcher .
Their mouth is full of curses and bitterness .
Grief and unhappiness are in their ways ; and the way of peace , they have not known .
13:7 Will they never learn : all those who work iniquity , who devour my people like a meal of bread ?
There , they have trembled in fear , where there was no fear .
You have confounded the counsel of the needy because the Lord is his hope .
When the Lord turns away the captivity of his people , Jacob will exult , and Israel will rejoice .
O Lord , who will dwell in your tabernacle ?
14:4 In his sight , the malicious one has been reduced to nothing , but he glorifies those who fear the Lord .
14:5 He who has not given his money in usury , nor accepted bribes against the innocent .
15:4 Their infirmities have been multiplied ; after this , they acted more quickly .
15:5 The Lord is the portion of my inheritance and my cup .
15:6 The lots have fallen upon me with clarity .
15:7 I will bless the Lord , who has bestowed understanding upon me .
15:8 I have made provision for the Lord always in my sight .
15:10 For you will not abandon my soul to Hell , nor will you allow your holy one to see corruption .
At your right hand are delights , even to the end .
Lord , listen to my justice , attend to my supplication .
16:2 Let my judgment proceed from your presence .
16:3 You have tested my heart and visited it by night .
16:5 Perfect my steps in your paths , so that my footsteps may not be disturbed .
Incline your ear to me and heed my words .
16:8 From those who resist your right hand , preserve me like the pupil of your eye .
16:10 They have concealed their fatness ; their mouth has been speaking arrogantly .
I will be satisfied when your glory appears .
For David , the servant of the Lord , who spoke the words of this canticle to the Lord , in the day that the Lord delivered him from the hand of all his enemies and from the hand of Saul .
My God is my helper , and I hope in him : my protector , and the horn of my salvation , and my support .
And I will be saved from my enemies .
17:6 The sorrows of Hell encompassed me , and the snares of death intercepted me .
And he listened to my voice from his holy temple .
17:9 A smoke ascended by his wrath , and a fire flared up from his face : coals were kindled by it .
And darkness was under his feet .
17:12 And he set darkness as his hiding place , with his tabernacle all around him : dark waters in the clouds of the air .
17:14 And the Lord thundered from heaven , and the Most High uttered his voice : hail and coals of fire .
He multiplied lightnings , and he set them in disarray .
17:18 He rescued me from my strongest enemies , and from those who hated me .
17:19 They intercepted me in the day of my affliction , and the Lord became my protector .
He accomplished my salvation , because he willed me .
17:28 For you will save the humble people , but you will bring down the eyes of the arrogant .
My God , enlighten my darkness .
He is the protector of all who hope in him .
17:34 It is he who has perfected my feet , like the feet of deer , and who stations me upon the heights .
And you have set my arms like a bow of brass .
And your right hand sustains me .
And your discipline itself will teach me .
17:38 I will pursue my enemies and apprehend them .
17:40 And you have wrapped me with virtue for the battle .
17:41 And you have given the back of my enemies to me , and you have destroyed those who hated me .
You will set me at the head of the Gentiles .
As soon as their ears heard , they were obedient to me .
17:49 And you will exalt me above those who rise up against me .
18:2 The heavens describe the glory of God , and the firmament announces the work of his hands .
18:4 There are no speeches or conversations , where their voices are not being heard .
18:6 He has placed his tabernacle in the sun , and he is like a bridegroom coming out of his bedroom .
18:7 his departure is from the summit of heaven .
Neither is there anyone who can hide himself from his heat .
The testimony of the Lord is faithful , providing wisdom to little ones .
The judgments of the Lord are true , justified in themselves :
From my hidden faults , cleanse me , O Lord ,
19:2 May the Lord hear you in the day of tribulation .
19:5 May he grant to you according to your heart , and confirm all your counsels .
19:7 May the Lord fulfill all your petitions .
He will hear him from his holy heaven .
19:8 Some trust in chariots , and some in horses , but we will call upon the name of the Lord our God .
But we have risen up , and we have been set upright .
20:2 In your virtue , Lord , the king will rejoice , and over your salvation , he will exult exceedingly .
20:4 For you have gone ahead of him with blessings of sweetness .
20:5 He petitioned you for life , and you have granted him length of days , in the present time , and forever and ever .
You will make him rejoice with gladness in your presence .
20:11 You will destroy their fruit from the earth and their offspring from the sons of men .
20:13 For you will make them turn their back ; with your remnants , you will prepare their countenance .
We will play music and sing psalms to your virtues .
For the tasks of early morning .
Far from my salvation are the words of my offenses .
They hoped , and you freed them .
In you , they hoped and were not confounded .
21:10 For you are the one who has drawn me out of the womb , my hope from the breasts of my mother .
21:13 Many calves have surrounded me ; fat bulls have besieged me .
21:16 My strength has dried up like clay , and my tongue has adhered to my jaws .
They have pierced my hands and feet .
And they have examined me and stared at me .
21:22 Save me from the mouth of the lion , and my humility from the horns of single-horned beast .
In the midst of the Church , I will praise you .
For he has neither spurned nor despised the pleas of the poor .
And when I cried out to him , he heeded me .
I will pay my vows in the sight of those who fear him .
Their hearts will live forever and ever .
You have anointed my head with oil , and my cup , which inebriates me , how brilliant it is !
The earth and all its fullness belong to the Lord : the whole world and all that dwells in it .
23:3 Who will ascend to the mountain of the Lord ?
23:4 The innocent of hands and the clean of heart , who has not received his soul in vain , nor sworn deceitfully to his neighbor .
23:6 This is the generation that seeks him , that seeks the face of the God of Jacob .
And the King of Glory shall enter .
The Lord who is strong and powerful ; the Lord powerful in battle .
The Lord of virtue .
Let me not be put to shame .
For all who remain with you will not be confounded .
O Lord , demonstrate your ways to me , and teach me your paths .
For you are God , my Saviour , and I remain with you all day long .
24:7 Do not remember the offenses of my youth and my ignorances .
24:10 All the ways of the Lord are mercy and truth , to those who yearn for his covenant and his testimonies .
24:13 His soul will dwell upon good things , and his offspring will inherit the earth .
24:17 The troubles of my heart have been multiplied .
24:18 See my lowliness and my hardship , and release all my offenses .
24:21 The innocent and the righteous have adhered to me , because I have remained with you .
Judge me , Lord , for I have been walking in my innocence , and by hoping in the Lord , I will not be weakened .
25:5 I have hated the assembly of the malicious ; and I will not sit with the impious .
The Lord is the protector of my life , of whom shall I be afraid ?
Those who trouble me , my enemies , have themselves been weakened and have fallen .
If a battle were to rise up against me , I would have hope in this .
26:6 He has exalted me upon the rock , and now he has exalted my head above my enemies .
26:14 Wait for the Lord , act manfully ; and let your heart be strengthened , and remain with the Lord .
For if you remain silent toward me , I will become like those who descend into the pit .
27:3 Do not draw me away together with sinners ; and let me not perish with those who work iniquity , who speak peacefully to their neighbor , yet evils are in their hearts .
Assign to them according to the works of their hands .
27:5 Since they have not understood the works of the Lord and the works of his hands , you will destroy them , and you will not build them up .
And my flesh has flourished again .
28:1 A Psalm of David , at the completion of the tabernacle .
Adore the Lord in his holy court .
28:6 And it will break them into pieces , like a calf of Lebanon , and in the same way as the beloved son of the single-horned beast .
28:9 The voice of the Lord is preparing the stags , and he will reveal the dense woods .
29:2 I will extol you , Lord , for you have sustained me , and you have not allowed my enemies to delight over me .
29:5 Sing a psalm to the Lord , you his saints , and confess with remembrance of his holiness .
29:10 What use would there be in my blood , if I descend into corruption ?
29:12 You have turned my mourning into gladness for me .
Be for me a protector God and a house of refuge , so as to accomplish my salvation .
30:7 You have hated those who practice emptiness to no purpose .
30:9 And you have not enclosed me in the hands of the enemy .
30:11 For my life has fallen into sorrow , and my years into sighing .
30:12 I have become a disgrace among all my enemies , and even more so to my neighbors , and a dread to my acquaintances .
30:14 For I have heard the harsh criticism of many who linger in the area .
30:19 May deceitful lips be silenced : those that speak iniquity against the just , in arrogance and in abusiveness .
30:21 You hide them in the concealment of your face , from the disturbance of men .
30:23 But I said in the excess of my mind : “I have been cast away from the glance of your eyes.” And so , you heeded the voice of my prayer , while I was still crying out to you .
31:1 The understanding of David himself .
31:2 Blessed is the man to whom the Lord has not imputed sin , and in whose spirit there is no deceit .
31:5 I have acknowledged my offense to you , and I have not concealed my injustice .
31:7 You are my refuge from the tribulation that has surrounded me .
31:8 I will give you understanding , and I will instruct you in this way , in which you will walk .
31:9 Do not become like the horse and the mule , which have no understanding .
31:10 Many are the scourges of the sinner , but mercy will surround him that hopes in the Lord .
32:2 Confess to the Lord with stringed instruments ; sing psalms to him with the psaltery , the instrument of ten strings .
Sing psalms to him skillfully , with loud exclamation .
32:6 By the word of the Lord , the heavens were established , and all their power , by the Spirit of his mouth :
32:8 Let all the earth fear the Lord , and may all the inhabitants of the world quake before him .
He commanded , and they were created .
Moreover , he reproves the thoughts of the people , and he rejects the counsels of the leaders .
32:12 Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord , the people whom he has chosen as his inheritance .
He has seen all the sons of men .
32:15 He has formed the hearts of each one of them ; he understands all their works .
32:17 The horse is false safety ; for he will not be saved by the abundance of his powers .
For he is our helper and protector .
33:6 Approach him and be enlightened , and your faces will not be confounded .
33:8 The Angel of the Lord will encamp around those who fear him , and he will rescue them .
Blessed is the man who hopes in him .
For there is no destitution for those who fear him .
I will teach you the fear of the Lord .
Inquire about peace , and pursue it .
33:17 But the countenance of the Lord is upon those who do evil , to perish the remembrance of them from the earth .
33:19 The Lord is near to those who are troubled in heart , and he will save the humble in spirit .
33:21 The Lord preserves all of their bones , not one of them shall be broken .
33:23 The Lord will redeem the souls of his servants , and none of those who hope in him will fare badly .
O Lord , judge those who harm me ; assail those who attack me .
34:3 Bring forth the spear , and close in on those who persecute me .
34:5 May they become like dust before the face of the wind , and let the Angel of the Lord hem them in .
34:7 For , without cause , they have concealed their snare for me unto destruction .
34:8 Let the snare , of which he is ignorant , come upon him , and let the deception , which he has hidden , take hold of him : and may he fall into that very snare .
34:10 All my bones will say , “Lord , who is like you ? ” He rescues the needy from the hand of the stronger one , the indigent and the poor from those who plunder him .
I humbled my soul with fasting , and my prayer will become my sinews .
34:15 And they have been joyful against me , and they joined together .
They scoffed at me with scorn .
34:19 May those who are my unjust adversaries not be glad over me : those who have hated me without cause , and who nod agreement with their eyes .
Let them be clothed with confusion and awe , who speak great things against me .
34:28 And so my tongue will express your justice : your praise all day long .
To the servant of the Lord , David himself .
There is no fear of God before his eyes .
35:4 The words of his mouth are iniquity and deceit .
Your judgments are a great abyss .
35:11 Extend your mercy before those who know you , and your justice to these , who are upright in heart .
36:4 Delight in the Lord , and he will grant to you the petitions of your heart .
36:6 And he will bring forth your justice like the light , and your judgment like the midday .
Do not choose to compete with him who prospers in his way , with the man who does injustice .
But those who remain with the Lord , these will inherit the land .
And you will search his place and find nothing .
36:12 The sinner will observe the just , and he will gnash his teeth over him .
36:14 The sinners have drawn the sword , they have bent their bow , so as to cast down the poor and the needy , so as to massacre the upright of heart .
36:18 The Lord knows the days of the immaculate , and their inheritance will be in eternity .
36:21 The sinner will lend and not release , but the just one shows compassion and donates .
36:25 I have been young , and now I am old ; and I have not seen the just forsaken , nor his offspring seeking bread .
They will be kept safe in eternity .
36:29 But the just will inherit the earth , and they will dwell upon it forever and ever .
36:33 But the Lord will not abandon him into his hands , nor condemn him , when he will be judged .
And I sought him , and his place was not found .
37:1 A Psalm of David , in commemoration of the Sabbath .
37:3 For your arrows have been driven into me , and your hand has been confirmed over me .
There is no peace for my bones before the face of my sins .
I have walked with contrition all day long .
37:9 I have been afflicted and greatly humbled .
My strength has abandoned me , and the light of my eyes has abandoned me , and it is not with me .
And those who were next to me stood far apart .
37:13 And those who sought evil accusations against me were speaking emptiness .
37:18 For I have been prepared for scourges , and my sorrow is ever before me .
37:21 Those who render evil for good have dragged me down , because I followed goodness .
38:3 I was silenced and humbled , and I was quiet before good things , and my sorrow was renewed .
Yet truly , all things are vanity : every living man .
He stores up , and he knows not for whom he will gather these things .
Is it not the Lord ?
38:12 I fall short at corrections from the strength of your hand .
And you have made his soul shrink away like a spider .
A Psalm of David himself .
39:3 And he heard my prayers and he led me out of the pit of misery and the quagmire .
39:5 Blessed is the man whose hope is in the name of the Lord , and who has no respect for vanities and absurd falsehoods .
I have announced and I have spoken : they are multiplied beyond number .
But you have perfected ears for me .
39:10 I have announced your justice in a great Church : behold , I will not restrain my lips .
39:11 I have not concealed your justice within my heart .
I have not concealed your mercy and your truth from a great assembly .
Your mercy and your truth ever sustain me .
My iniquities have taken hold of me , and I was not able to see .
And my heart has forsaken me .
You are my helper and my protector .
40:2 Blessed is he who shows understanding toward the needy and the poor .
40:3 May the Lord preserve him and give him life , and make him blessed upon the earth .
40:6 My enemies have spoken evils against me .
He went outside , and he was speaking in the same way .
Will he that sleeps no longer rise again ?
40:12 By this , I knew that you preferred me : because my adversary will not rejoice over me .
40:14 Blessed is the Lord God of Israel , for all generations and even forever .
The understanding of the sons of Korah .
41:3 My soul has thirsted for the strong living God .
Hope in God , for I will still confess to him : the salvation of my countenance ,
My soul has been troubled within myself .
41:8 Abyss calls upon abyss , with the voice of your floodgate .
And why do I walk in mourning , while my adversary afflicts me ? ”
Meanwhile , they say to me every single day , “Where is your God ?
And why do I walk in sadness , while the adversary afflicts me ?
They have guided me and led me , to your holy mountain and into your tabernacles .
To you , O God , my God , I will confess upon a stringed instrument .
43:3 Your hand dispersed the Gentiles , and you transplanted them .
43:4 For they did not take possession of the land by their sword , and their own arm did not save them .
43:5 You yourself are my king and my God , who commands the salvation of Jacob .
43:11 You have turned our back to our enemies , and those who hated us have plundered for themselves .
You have scattered us among the Gentiles .
43:14 You have set us as a disgrace to our neighbors , a scoff and a derision to those who are around us .
43:16 All day long my shame is before me , and the confusion of my face has covered me ,
43:18 All these things have come upon us , yet we have not forgotten you , and we have not acted unjustly in your covenant .
And you have not diverted our steps from your way .
43:21 If we have forgotten the name of our God , and if we have extended our hands to a foreign god ,
For he knows the secrets of the heart .
We are considered as sheep for the slaughter .
43:24 Why do you turn your face away , and why do you forget our needfulness and our tribulation ?
Our belly has been bound to the earth .
Help us and redeem us , because of your name .
For those who will be changed .
I speak of my works to the king .
44:3 You are a brilliant form before the sons of men .
Because of this , God has blessed you in eternity .
44:5 With your splendor and your excellence extended , proceed prosperously , and reign for the sake of truth and meekness and justice , and so will your right hand lead you wondrously .
44:8 You have loved justice and hated iniquity .
44:13 And the daughters of Tyre will entreat your countenance with gifts : all the rich men of the people .
Her neighbors will be brought to you .
They will be led into the temple of the king .
You will establish them as leaders over all the earth .
Because of this , people will confess to you in eternity , even forever and ever .
To the sons of Korah , for confidants .
45:2 Our God is our refuge and strength , a helper in the tribulations that have greatly overwhelmed us .
45:4 They thundered , and the waters were stirred up among them ; the mountains have been disturbed by his strength .
The Most High has sanctified his tabernacle .
God will assist it in the early morning .
He uttered his voice : the earth has been moved .
The God of Jacob is our supporter .
46:3 For the Lord is exalted and terrible : a great King over all the earth .
46:5 He has chosen us for his inheritance : the splendor of Jacob , whom he has loved .
46:10 The leaders of the peoples have been gathered together by the God of Abraham .
47:2 The Lord is great and exceedingly praiseworthy , in the city of our God , on his holy mountain .
47:6 Such did they see , and they were astonished : they were disturbed , they were moved .
In that place , their pains were that of a woman in labor .
Your right hand is full of justice .
48:7 Those who trust in their own strength and who glory in the multitude of their riches ,
He will not give to God his appeasement ,
48:11 He will not see death , when he sees the wise dying : the foolish and the senseless will perish together .
48:12 And their sepulchers will be their houses forever , their tabernacles from generation to generation .
And the just will have dominion over them in the morning .
48:18 For when he dies , he will take nothing away , and his glory will not descend with him .
48:20 He will even enter with the progeny of his fathers , but , even in eternity , he will not see the light .
He has been compared to the senseless beasts , and he has become like them .
The God of gods , the Lord has spoken , and he has called the earth , from the rising of the sun even to its setting ,
A fire will flare up in his sight , and a mighty tempest will surround him .
49:5 Gather his holy ones to him , you who order his covenant above sacrifices .
Listen , Israel , and I will testify for you .
49:8 I will not reprove you for your sacrifices .
49:9 I will not accept calves from your house , nor he-goats from your flocks .
49:14 Offer to God the sacrifice of praise , and pay your vows to the Most High .
I will rescue you , and you will honor me .
49:17 Truly , you have hated discipline , and you have cast my sermons behind you .
49:19 Your mouth has abounded with malice , and your tongue has concocted deceits .
But I will reprove you , and I will set myself against your face .
50:2 when Nathan the prophet came to him , after he went to Bathsheba .
And so , you are justified in your words , and you will prevail when you give judgment .
50:9 You will sprinkle me with hyssop , and I will be cleansed .
50:10 In my hearing , you will grant gladness and rejoicing .
50:15 I will teach the unjust your ways , and the impious will be converted to you .
Then they will lay calves upon your altar .
The understanding of David .
